    "cost_closing_html":  "About \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}} a bowl\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost). The pork shoulder is nearly all of it. The sweet potato that holds the whole thing together is the cheapest item on the list.",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eSweet potatoes are cheapest loose by the pound in fall.\u003c/strong\u003e Look for ones that are even in thickness rather than the biggest in the bin, because they roast through at the same rate.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eBuy a bone-in pork shoulder and slow cook it whole.\u003c/strong\u003e It is the lowest cost per pound of protein in the meat case and the bone makes the juices better.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eBarbecue sauce is worth making from pantry staples if you have them.\u003c/strong\u003e If not, buy the store brand. One bottle covers this batch with plenty to spare.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eStore the pork and the potatoes in separate containers.\u003c/strong\u003e The potato reheats better on its own and does not go soggy under sauce all week. It costs nothing to split them."
